Why this file exists
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Not because a license clause demands it.

This package renders through `lightweight-charts`, which is Apache-2.0 and carries
`Copyright 2023 TradingView, Inc.` Clause 4(d) of that license only obliges a
downstream NOTICE when the upstream work "includes a NOTICE text file as part of
its distribution" -- and, measured against `lightweight-charts` 5.2.0, it ships no
NOTICE at all: the published tarball contains `LICENSE`, `README.md`,
`package.json` and the build output, nothing more. On top of that, this package
does not redistribute `lightweight-charts`; it declares the library as a required
peer dependency, so the consumer installs it directly from TradingView and never
receives a copy from us. There is no Derivative Work here to attach a notice to.

The file exists because the *name* does. `lightweight-magic-charts` echoes
`lightweight-charts` on purpose -- it is meant to read as "the workspace you build
on top of that renderer" -- and a name that close invites the reader to assume a
relationship that does not exist. Apache-2.0 grants no trademark rights (clause 6)
and offers no protection against confusion of origin, so the disclaimer has to be
written down somewhere. This is that place.

